      "id": "G37",
      "description": "cmd_drift crashed (TypeError, unpacking None) when a holding's cluster had no policy target (band_pct: None) -- the 'Unclassified' cluster case was represented in cluster_table but the later breach-testing loop assumed every cluster had a real band. Never hit before because every previously-held ticker already had a sector_map entry; BE (new position, first-ever hold) was the first to reach this path. Fixed same session: unclassified clusters now skip the breach test instead of crashing the whole subcommand.",
      "opened": "2026-07-29",
